---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Home"
  description="Meet John Hendrix — the Prophet of Oak Ridge, Tennessee, whose extraordinary visions foretold the Manhattan Project of World War II."
>

  <!-- Hero -->
  <section class="bg-forest-textured text-parchment hero-border">
    <div class="section-container py-24 sm:py-32 pl-8 sm:pl-12">
      <span class="eyebrow-light">Oak Ridge, Tennessee · Est. 1942</span>
      <h1 class="font-display text-hero text-parchment mb-3 leading-tight">
        The <em class="italic text-copper-light">Prophet</em><br />of Oak Ridge
      </h1>
      <p class="font-display italic text-stone-light text-lg mb-8">
        A farmer. Forty nights. A prophecy fulfilled.
      </p>
      <p class="text-parchment-dark text-lg max-w-xl mb-10 leading-relaxed font-body">
        A simple East Tennessee farmer spent forty nights sleeping in the woods — and emerged
        with visions that foretold the Manhattan Project, decades before the atomic age began.
      </p>
      <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-4">
        <a href="/prayerwalk" class="btn-donate">Walk the Trail</a>
        <a href="/donate" class="inline-block bg-transparent text-parchment font-ui font-semibold px-6 py-3 rounded-sm border-2 border-forest-light hover:bg-forest-light transition-colors duration-200 min-h-[48px]">Support the Vision</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Copper divider -->
  <div class="copper-divider"></div>

  <!-- John's Story: Timeline + Sticky Video Sidebar -->
  <section class="section-pad bg-parchment">
    <div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      <span class="eyebrow">His Story</span>
      <h2 class="font-display text-section text-forest mb-10">Meet John Hendrix</h2>

      <div class="grid lg:grid-cols-5 gap-12 lg:gap-10 items-start">

        <!-- Timeline (left, wider column) -->
        <div class="lg:col-span-3">
          <ol class="relative border-l-2 border-copper/30 pl-8 space-y-10">

            <li class="relative">
              <span class="absolute -left-[calc(2rem+7px)] top-1 w-3 h-3 rounded-full bg-copper"></span>
              <span class="font-ui text-copper text-sm font-semibold tracking-wide">1900</span>
              <h3 class="font-display text-xl text-forest mb-2">The Tragedy</h3>
              <p class="text-ink-soft leading-relaxed">
                John Hendrix and his wife Julia had five children when diphtheria hit their community
                around the turn of the 20th century. Baby Ethel got sick and died. The family was turned
                upside down with turmoil. Julia couldn't cope with her grief, so she took the other children
                and boarded a wagon headed for Arkansas — after which John never saw any of them again.
              </p>
            </li>

            <li class="relative">
              <span class="absolute -left-[calc(2rem+7px)] top-1 w-3 h-3 rounded-full bg-copper"></span>
              <span class="font-ui text-copper text-sm font-semibold tracking-wide">1901</span>
              <h3 class="font-display text-xl text-forest mb-2">Forty Nights in the Woods</h3>
              <p class="text-ink-soft leading-relaxed">
                As people often do during a time of trial, John began asking God why this was happening to him.
                He took long walks in the woods of his property praying for understanding. One day while in the
                woods he heard a thunderous voice promise that if he would sleep with his head on the ground for
                forty nights, he would be shown the future of his land. So he did it. He chose a spot near a
                fence row. Neighbors brought him soup and covered him with blankets. One cold morning someone
                found him with his hair frozen to the ground.
              </p>
            </li>

            <li class="relative">
              <span class="absolute -left-[calc(2rem+7px)] top-1 w-3 h-3 rounded-full bg-copper"></span>
              <span class="font-ui text-copper text-sm font-semibold tracking-wide">1901</span>
              <h3 class="font-display text-xl text-forest mb-2">The Visions</h3>
              <p class="text-ink-soft leading-relaxed">
                Forty days later John reappeared from the woods and said he had been shown visions of the future.
                He said a city would be built on Black Oak Ridge for thousands of people. He said big factories
                would be built down in Bear Creek Valley where they would be "building things." He said what was
                going to be built would help win one of the greatest wars that would ever be.
              </p>
            </li>

            <li class="relative">
              <span class="absolute -left-[calc(2rem+7px)] top-1 w-3 h-3 rounded-full bg-copper"></span>
              <span class="font-ui text-copper text-sm font-semibold tracking-wide">1942</span>
              <h3 class="font-display text-xl text-forest mb-2">The Fulfillment</h3>
              <p class="text-ink-soft leading-relaxed">
                In 1915 John Hendrix died of tuberculosis. In 1942, the War Department seized this primitive
                community — still without electricity — for a war emergency. People who had heard John's
                predictions finally understood what he had seen in those forty nights in the woods.
              </p>
              <div class="pullquote mt-6">
                <p>"I guess ol' John wasn't crazy after all."</p>
                <cite>— John's neighbors, 1942</cite>
              </div>
            </li>

          </ol>
        </div>

        <!-- Sidebar: video + CTA (right, narrower column, sticky on desktop) -->
        <div class="lg:col-span-2 lg:sticky lg:top-24">
          <div
            class="relative w-full bg-ink rounded-sm overflow-hidden"
            style="padding-bottom: 56.25%;"
            data-youtube-id="BdaB8fVaIps"
            id="youtube-embed"
          >
            <div id="youtube-placeholder" class="absolute inset-0 flex items-center justify-center cursor-pointer group">
              <img
                src="https://img.youtube.com/vi/BdaB8fVaIps/hqdefault.jpg"
                alt="Documentary film about John Hendrix, the Prophet of Oak Ridge"
                class="absolute inset-0 w-full h-full object-cover opacity-80"
                loading="lazy"
              />
              <div class="relative z-10 w-16 h-16 bg-copper rounded-full flex items-center justify-center group-hover:bg-copper-light transition-colors shadow-lg">
                <i class="ti ti-player-play text-parchment text-2xl ml-0.5" aria-hidden="true"></i>
              </div>
            </div>
            <iframe
              id="youtube-iframe"
              class="absolute inset-0 w-full h-full hidden"
              src=""
              title="John Hendrix documentary film"
              frameborder="0"
              allow="accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture"
              allowfullscreen
            ></iframe>
          </div>
          <p class="text-stone font-ui text-sm mt-3">
            Portrayed by Jack Mansfield. Video courtesy of Secret City Films.
          </p>
          <a href="/prayerwalk" class="btn-donate w-full text-center mt-6 block">
            <i class="ti ti-map-pin mr-2" aria-hidden="true"></i>Walk the Trail
          </a>
        </div>

      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- CTA strip -->
  <section class="bg-forest-textured text-parchment py-16">
    <div class="section-container text-center">
      <h2 class="font-display text-2xl text-parchment mb-3">Walk Where John Walked</h2>
      <p class="text-parchment-dark mb-8 max-w-md mx-auto leading-relaxed">
        The ½-mile Memorial Prayer Walk along Hendrix Creek is free and open to all visitors.
      </p>
      <a href="/find-us" class="btn-donate">
        <i class="ti ti-map-pin mr-2" aria-hidden="true"></i>Get Directions
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>

</Layout>

<script>
  const placeholder = document.getElementById('youtube-placeholder');
  const iframe = document.getElementById('youtube-iframe') as HTMLIFrameElement | null;
  const embedDiv = document.getElementById('youtube-embed');

  placeholder?.addEventListener('click', () => {
    if (iframe && embedDiv) {
      const videoId = embedDiv.dataset.youtubeId;
      iframe.src = `https://www.youtube.com/embed/${videoId}?autoplay=1`;
      iframe.classList.remove('hidden');
      placeholder.classList.add('hidden');
    }
  });
</script>